    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 2,
      "title": "Locks: Basic idea",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Locks: Basic idea",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 247.9,
          "cw": 17.41
        },
        {
          "text": "• Consider update of shared variable",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.255,
          "bottom": 0.316,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "• We can use a special lock variable to protect it",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.361,
          "bottom": 0.422,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "• All threads accessing a critical section share a lock",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.626,
          "bottom": 0.686,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "• One threads succeeds in locking – owner of lock",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.678,
          "bottom": 0.739,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "• Other threads that try to lock cannot proceed further",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.731,
          "bottom": 0.792,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "until lock is released by the owner",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.779,
          "bottom": 0.835,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 10.65
        },
        {
          "text": "• Pthreads library in Linux provides such locks",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.827,
          "bottom": 0.888,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 3,
      "title": "Building a lock",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Building a lock",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 267.3,
          "cw": 17.14
        },
        {
          "text": "• Goals of a lock implementation",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.218,
          "bottom": 0.29,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "– Mutual exclusion (obviously!)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.287,
          "bottom": 0.35,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 15.55
        },
        {
          "text": "– Fairness: all threads should eventually get the",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.347,
          "bottom": 0.41,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 15.55
        },
        {
          "text": "lock, and no thread should starve",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.402,
          "bottom": 0.46,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 11.44
        },
        {
          "text": "Low overhead: acquiring, releasing, and waiting",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.462,
          "bottom": 0.52,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 11.5
        },
        {
          "text": "for lock should not consume too many resources",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.512,
          "bottom": 0.57,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 11.99
        },
        {
          "text": "• Implementation of locks are needed for both",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.567,
          "bottom": 0.639,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "userspace programs (e.g., pthreads library)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.629,
          "bottom": 0.696,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.93
        },
        {
          "text": "and kernel code",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.686,
          "bottom": 0.752,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 13.79
        },
        {
          "text": "• Implementing locks needs support from",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.749,
          "bottom": 0.821,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "hardware and OS",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.811,
          "bottom": 0.878,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 14.91
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Is disabling interrupts enough?",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Is disabling interrupts enough?",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 120.5,
          "cw": 17.75
        },
        {
          "text": "• Is this enough?",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.258,
          "bottom": 0.326,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "• No, not always!",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.323,
          "bottom": 0.39,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "• Many issues here:",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.387,
          "bottom": 0.455,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "– Disabling interrupts is a privileged instruction and",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.452,
          "bottom": 0.511,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "program can misuse it (e.g., run forever)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.503,
          "bottom": 0.557,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.33
        },
        {
          "text": "– Will not work on multiprocessor systems, since",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.554,
          "bottom": 0.613,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "another thread on another core can enter critical",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.605,
          "bottom": 0.659,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.54
        },
        {
          "text": "section",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.651,
          "bottom": 0.705,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.88
        },
        {
          "text": "• This technique is used to implement locks on",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.702,
          "bottom": 0.77,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "single processor systems inside the OS",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.76,
          "bottom": 0.822,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.23
        },
        {
          "text": "– Need better solution for other situations",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.82,
          "bottom": 0.878,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 5,
      "title": "A failed lock implementation (1)",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "A failed lock implementation (1)",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 110.2,
          "cw": 17.85
        },
        {
          "text": "• Lock: spin on a flag variable until it is unset,",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.214,
          "bottom": 0.287,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "then set it to acquire lock",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.283,
          "bottom": 0.349,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.2
        },
        {
          "text": "• Unlock: unset flag variable",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.352,
          "bottom": 0.425,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 6,
      "title": "A failed lock implementation (2)",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "A failed lock implementation (2)",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 110.2,
          "cw": 17.85
        },
        {
          "text": "• Thread 1 spins, lock is released, ends spin",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.214,
          "bottom": 0.287,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "• Thread 1 interrupted just before setting flag",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.29,
          "bottom": 0.362,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "• Race condition has moved to the lock",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.365,
          "bottom": 0.437,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "acquisition code!",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.434,
          "bottom": 0.5,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 13.06
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 7,
      "title": "Solution: Hardware atomic instructions",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Solution: Hardware atomic instructions",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.127,
          "bottom": 0.21,
          "x0": 79.6,
          "cw": 16.63
        },
        {
          "text": "• Very hard to ensure atomicity only in software",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.263,
          "bottom": 0.336,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "• Modern architectures provide hardware",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.339,
          "bottom": 0.411,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "atomic instructions",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.407,
          "bottom": 0.474,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 13.08
        },
        {
          "text": "• Example of an atomic instruction: test-and-set",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.477,
          "bottom": 0.549,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "– Update a variable and return old value, all in one",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.551,
          "bottom": 0.614,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 15.55
        },
        {
          "text": "hardware instruction",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.611,
          "bottom": 0.669,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 11.85
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 8,
      "title": "Simple lock using test-and-set",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Simple lock using test-and-set",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 129.5,
          "cw": 17.76
        },
        {
          "text": "• If TestAndSet(flag,1) returns 1, it means the lock is held by",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.226,
          "bottom": 0.28,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 8.4
        },
        {
          "text": "someone else, so wait busily",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.277,
          "bottom": 0.327,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 9.88
        },
        {
          "text": "• This lock is called a spinlock – spins until lock is acquired",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.329,
          "bottom": 0.384,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 8.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 9,
      "title": "Spinlock using compare-and-swap",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Spinlock using compare-and-swap",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 92.3,
          "cw": 19.59
        },
        {
          "text": "• Another atomic instruction: compare-and-swap",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.263,
          "bottom": 0.336,
          "x0": 67.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "• Spinlock using compare-and-swap",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.565,
          "bottom": 0.637,
          "x0": 67.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Alternative to spinning",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Alternative to spinning",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 193.3,
          "cw": 17.61
        },
        {
          "text": "• Alternative to spinlock: a (sleeping) mutex",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.215,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.79
        },
        {
          "text": "• Instead of spinning for a lock, a contending thread",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.281,
          "bottom": 0.344,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.79
        },
        {
          "text": "could simply give up the CPU and check back later",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.341,
          "bottom": 0.399,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 11.56
        },
        {
          "text": "– yield() moves thread from running to ready state",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.4,
          "bottom": 0.454,
          "x0": 128.5,
          "cw": 13.75
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 11,
      "title": "Spinlock vs. sleeping mutex",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Spinlock vs. sleeping mutex",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 152.1,
          "cw": 18.06
        },
        {
          "text": "• Most userspace lock implementations are of the",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.226,
          "bottom": 0.286,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "sleeping mutex kind",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.273,
          "bottom": 0.329,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 11.52
        },
        {
          "text": "– CPU wasted by spinning contending threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.321,
          "bottom": 0.376,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "– More so if a thread holds spinlock and blocks for long",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.368,
          "bottom": 0.423,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• Locks inside the OS are always spinlocks",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.415,
          "bottom": 0.476,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "– Why? Who will the OS yield to?",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.468,
          "bottom": 0.523,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• When OS acquires a spinlock:",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.515,
          "bottom": 0.576,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "– It must disable interrupts (on that processor core) while",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.568,
          "bottom": 0.623,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "the lock is held. Why? An interrupt handler could request",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.61,
          "bottom": 0.66,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 9.75
        },
        {
          "text": "the same lock, and spin for it forever.",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.648,
          "bottom": 0.698,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 9.21
        },
        {
          "text": "– It must not perform any blocking operation – never go to",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.691,
          "bottom": 0.745,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "sleep with a locked spinlock!",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.733,
          "bottom": 0.783,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 9.56
        },
        {
          "text": "• In general, use spinlocks with care, and release as soon",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.775,
          "bottom": 0.836,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "as possible",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.822,
          "bottom": 0.878,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 10.81
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 12,
      "title": "How should locks be used?",
      "images": 15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "How should locks be used?",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 155.1,
          "cw": 19.25
        },
        {
          "text": "• A lock should be acquired before accessing any",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.253,
          "bottom": 0.321,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "variable or data structure that is shared between",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.306,
          "bottom": 0.368,
          "x0": 106.2,
